result:
Phase-06 (US4, Todo Plans) passed all 15 API checks on attempt 1, and the verdict is **pass**.

- **Checks:** I wrote a new test plan, `loops/testing/outputs/001-quickflow/backend-dev/phase-06-test.md`, covering AC-US4-1..8 and 10..12, the FR-07 limits and the swagger. It passed on:
  - creating a plan with its items;
  - rejecting a plan with no items, a missing or deleted item, or an end time at or before the start;
  - progress as done items over total;
  - marking a task item done completes the task, while un-ticking it or ticking a habit or learning item changes nothing;
  - status and rest time computed from the stored times and the current time;
  - list grouping and ordering as the contract states;
  - items whose source was deleted stay in the plan and still count;
  - deleting a plan leaves its tasks, habits and cards unchanged;
  - the swagger lists all six plan operations and the eight schemas.
- **How they ran:** as in phase-05, the session's permissions blocked running `phase-06-verify.sh`. So I ran the same checks as direct curl calls. Every response is saved in `loops/testing/runs/001-quickflow/backend-dev/phase-06/attempt-1/http/`, and all of them are collected in `curl.log` there.
- **Unit tests:** 276 passed, 0 failed. The runner again reported coverage as "skipped": its gate looks for classes directly in `com/quickflow/domain`, and they are all in sub-packages. From `jacoco.csv`, domain line coverage is 96.2% (590/613), above the 80% threshold.
- **Not covered:** FR-08.1, the notification when a plan's start time is reached, has no backend test or check. It belongs to the frontend layer (AC-US4-9). The Dashboard part of AC-US4-4 belongs to phase-07.

There are no open questions. I wrote the report (`phase-06-report.md`), the verdict (`verdicts/backend-dev/phase-06.json`) and one line in `loops/testing/progress.md`.
